<p>In the latest twist, the British government has forced out Foreign Office Permanent Under-Secretary Olly Robbins after disclosures that Peter Mandelson was granted Developed Vetting and allowed to become ambassador to the United States despite failing the vetting process recommended by the UK’s screening agency. The government said neither Prime Minister Keir Starmer nor other ministers knew until this week that Mandelson had received Developed Vetting against the agency’s advice, and Darren Jones said he had ordered an urgent review into how that happened. The disclosures have added to the pressure on Starmer because he had previously said a “full due process” had been followed in Mandelson’s appointment, leading opposition figures to ask whether Parliament was misled and to call for his resignation. The affair has also revived scrutiny of Mandelson’s links to Jeffrey Epstein, while some reports have pointed to concerns about his ties to China and Russia, turning the episode into a broader test of accountability and vetting standards inside the UK government.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/t-Ware-CK5DMNOORzW6YbR_wvOlmW2IhXOr0VIupd544VKuXWy1fhQMeTvH3u4SXZ8r1qxSfx5qIE50fCaz8zcpuS9bC9aWYWoBCaTScaP8y0Hu07u3vKMImRzyfbswd48GTc4Yv3QD7TcAASSDOaMdWxM5h0cbRTOC1VIKFFcBKLAE-SqWGhSaO4iOb8D8YuI04fpu1kueH91RCssEk7JT5ofPB6ln2CZvUeKoL8ZtMou59wGUFCLYwOVfmOPbJ61F_zg4Iyu2MO8vqnA' alt='Peter Mandelson leaves his home in north London, Wednesday March 11, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Departmental responsibility: The decision was made inside the Foreign Office when Robbins was its top official, focusing attention on internal sign-off, not just the politics of Mandelson’s appointment.</li><li>Confidence lost: Multiple outlets said Starmer and Foreign Secretary Yvette Cooper lost confidence in Robbins, directly tying his departure to the handling of the clearance decision.</li><li>Later fallout: Politico reported that Mandelson was removed from the ambassador role in September 2025 over his links to Jeffrey Epstein.</li><li>Separate investigation: SCMP reported that Mandelson is under police investigation over allegations that he leaked government documents to Jeffrey Epstein.</li></ul><blockquote>It is utterly unacceptable - Darren Jones</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>UK government: Downing Street has cast the affair as a breakdown in Foreign Office procedures, arguing that accountability should center on how the system allowed UKSV advice to be overridden without ministers knowing. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/keir-starmer-dismisses-top-official-olly-robbins-peter-mandelson-vetting-crisis-deepens/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>Liberal Democrats: Leader Ed Davey argued that Starmer should resign even if he learned of the override only this week, saying that would still point to negligence and weak control at the top of government. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/apr/17/peter-mandelson-keir-starmer-olly-robbins-vetting-foreign-office-latest-news-updates'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/17/uk-opposition-call-on-starmer-to-resign-following-new-revelations-around-epstein-associate-peter-mandelson_6752520_4.html'>Senior UK official steps down after Mandelson vetting scandal</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/16/world/europe/peter-mandelson-epstein-starmer-security.html'>Mandelson, a Friend of Epstein’s, Became U.S. Ambassador Despite Failing Security Vetting</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-mandelson-failed-security-vetting-for-ambassador-role/'>U.K PM Starmer faces calls to resign as government admits ambassador to U.S. failed vetting process</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/uks-starmer-faces-calls-to-resign-as-mandelson-row-reignites'>UK&#x27;s Starmer faces calls to r